 replaces it and /opt/unetlab/html/store does not exist on fresh installs.
 The web console (frontend + backend bridges + units) is built into this
 package as of 6.8.31 — the pnetlab-webconsole package is retired
 (Provides/Replaces/Conflicts it so it is removed cleanly on upgrade).
 .
 Ubuntu 26.04 (27H1 v8) Depends deltas vs the focal vendor package:
 lib32gcc1->lib32gcc-s1; ntp/ntpdate->chrony; libsdl1.2-compat->libsdl1.2debian
 (libsdl1.2-compat gone on 26.04); time64 renames libelf1->libelf1t64,
 libpcap0.8->libpcap0.8t64; dropped python2, uml-utilities, resolvconf,
 libtinfo5/libncurses5/libncursesw5 (IOL ncurses compat ships as a staged deps/
 deb). Stock Linux 7.0 carries in-tree KSM, so no custom kernel is pinned.
 .
 Added 2026-08-05: python3-httpx + python3-websockets. This package Provides
 pnetlab-webconsole and ships /opt/pnet-webconsole's bridges, so their python
 imports are THIS package's dependencies. Both were undeclared here; httpx
 arrived only incidentally via the installer's optional AI/MCP pip step, so an
 install that skipped it left pnet-http-bridge crash-looping on
 ModuleNotFoundError and every node web console AND Wireshark capture iframe
 rendered Apache's 503 page. Prefer the apt packages: pip installs under
 /usr/local shadow apt modules.
 .
 Added 2026-08-23: the legacy pnet-websockify.service and
 pnet-telnet-bridge.service were deliberately retired at a072c76, but an
 additive builder sync plus wildcard stage copy kept shipping them until
 6.8.67, where they failed with 203/EXEC. python3-websockify is deliberately
 not re-added; web-console unit staging is now an explicit allowlist with a
 build-time negative gate for retired units and backends.
 .
 Added 2026-08-23: dhcpcd-base is an explicit runtime dependency for the
 shipped /usr/sbin/pnetlab-netcfg CLI and pnetlab-netcfg-firstboot.service,
 which invoke dhcpcd on the first-boot network setup path.
 .
 Added 2026-08-24: iptables-persistent (Defect #A, D1's "L3 forwarding rules
 survive reboot" guarantee). Before this, every boot started with empty
 netfilter tables and only PNetLab's own reconciled rules came back --
 any admin-added iptables/ip6tables rule was silently lost. Ordering against
 pnet-fwd-reconcile.sh's own PNETLAB-FWD chain matters: see the drop-in at
 engine-custom/etc/systemd/system/pnetlab-ovfstartup.service.d/ and the
 comment above reconcile_iptables() in pnet-fwd-reconcile.sh. Installer/
 upgrade apt-get calls already run with DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive, so
 the package's debconf autosave question is answered from its own default,
 no explicit preseed needed. ebtables/L2 persistence is explicitly OUT OF
 SCOPE -- PNETLAB-L2 is reconciled fresh every boot by design, never
 admin-customizable; see D1 in docs/pass2-design/03-revised-plan.md.
