Package: pnetlab-docker
Version: 6.8.78resolute1
Name: PNETLab Docker
Architecture: amd64
Section: devel
Priority: optional
Maintainer: pnetlab.com
Homepage: http://www.pnetlab.com
Conflicts: eve-ng-dockers
Replaces: docker-engine, docker-ce
Pre-Depends:  docker-engine | docker-ce
Depends:  docker-engine | docker-ce, jq
Description: Docker PNETLab compatible
 Versioned to ENGINE_VERSION (debs/VERSION) since 6.8.63resolute1 so the package
 validates under debs/publish-codeberg.sh (distribution Phase 1); the content is
 the 6.0.0-31 docker-rebroker Stage 7 config deb, unchanged. 6.0.0-31 ->
 6.8.63resolute1 sorts forward, so the upgrade path is monotonic.
 .
 docker-rebroker Stage 7: daemon.json binds ONLY the unix socket
 (tcp://127.0.0.1:4243 retired) and enables live-restore so dockerd restarts
 do not bounce running lab containers. postinst no longer stops/prunes
 running containers (the 6.0.0-30 postinst did — destructive on upgrades).
 /etc/docker/daemon.json is jq-CONVERGED by the postinst from the reference
 defaults at /usr/share/pnetlab-docker/daemon.defaults.json: admin edits are
 preserved, hosts (unix-only) + live-restore are force-set, and dockerd is
 restarted only when those forced keys actually changed. Address pools default
 to 10.177.0.0/16 size 24 (256 networks).
